# A handshake in three phases. Every phase has its own clock and a deadline:
#   hello      must be answered within 4 time units   (clock a)
#   key        takes between 2 and 6 time units       (clock b)
#   confirm    must arrive within 3 time units        (clock c)
# Each clock only matters in its own phase. With one global bound (6) all three
# clocks are tracked up to 7 everywhere; with per-location bounds a clock is
# dropped as soon as nothing depends on it any more.
#   ./build/automata states examples/handshake.ta
clocks a b c
locations hello key confirm established
initial hello
invariant hello a<=4
invariant key b<=6
invariant confirm c<=3
edge hello key server_hello guard=a>=1 reset=b
edge key confirm key_exchange guard=b>=2 reset=c
edge confirm established finished guard=c>=1
